Removes draft 55's wait from `FolderState::unsettled` (8045510): a
revert no longer waits for a fresh observation of a path it would revert
whose latest observation was ignored while a want held it in flight, and
so never asks the host to `Observe` one. A revert then decides on a
record that describes neither the disk nor anything the engine saw: the
user's new file at a path whose deletion was pending survives it, unknown
to the index, and the next scan announces it (I9, "kept unknown file";
DESIGN.md §8.3).

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_revert_waits_to_observe_a_path_a_want_held
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_revert_asks_to_observe_a_path_a_want_held_and_waits_for_it
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_commit_report_is_the_fresh_observation_a_revert_waits_for
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_report_that_finds_the_path_as_recorded_is_a_fresh_observation

